Maybe it will help. One part of the error text is: `[image data sha1: Error hashin`. This occurs in `txt` variable many times. When I tried hashing something with the function used in `snapshot.R` in `shinytest`, it hashes properly. For example: `digest::digest("saol",algo="sha1", serialize = FALSE)` outputs: `"98b0e83ae8f5ca51bba1fed747a4a520faa847ec"`

In some applications, the user may need to specify the port which shinytest runs on, however shinytest uses `random_open_port()` to specify the port.

```
  port <- random_open_port()
  if (is_rmd(path)) {
    # Shiny document
    rcmd <- paste0(
      rcmd,
      "; options(shiny.testmode = TRUE); ",
      sprintf("rmarkdown::run('%s', shiny_args=list(port=%d))", path, port)
    )
  } else {
    # Normal shiny app
    rcmd <- paste0(
      rcmd,
      "; options(shiny.testmode = TRUE); ",
      sprintf("shiny::runApp('%s', port=%d)", path, port)
    )
  }
```
https://github.com/rstudio/shinytest/blob/master/R/initialize.R#L101-L116

Example: With shinyjs, there are some functions that do some R <-> JS message passing, and it looks like shinytest tries to record that

```
library(shiny)
shinyApp(
  ui = fluidPage(
    shinyjs::useShinyjs(),
    actionButton("btn", "Reset"),
    textInput("text", "text", "text")
  ),
  server = function(input, output) {
    observeEvent(input$btn, {
      shinyjs::reset("text")
    })
  }
)
```

When you click Reset, the recording app tries to record an internal message (it shows up in the table of actions recorded), although in the test script that gets generated it does say that "Input x was set, but doesn't have an input binding." (as per the Limitations section in the docs). It would be great to be able to mark the event as non-recordable.

Relevant code in shinyjs: https://github.com/daattali/shinyjs/blob/master/R/reset.R#L72-L76 https://github.com/daattali/shinyjs/blob/master/inst/srcjs/shinyjs-default-funcs.js#L769

For this app, the recorder will log an input change event when you click on the text, even before the text changes:

```R
library(shiny)

ui <- fluidPage(
  textInput("x", "text", "abc")
)
server <- function(input, output, session) {
  observeEvent(input$x, {
    cat("text: ", input$x, "\n")
  })
}
shinyApp(ui, server)
```

The problem is that the recorder's deduplication mechanism doesn't use the initial values; it only uses values that are sent by a `shiny:inputchanged` event. It should record the initial values as well.

@wch Capturing our exchange on Slack about this.

With an app with a DT (and probably other widgets or htmlwidgets), the `sessionId` and `nonce` from Shiny are some recorded as part of the DT's metadata ([example](https://github.com/rstudio/shinyTestResults/blob/master/apps/dt-test/tests/mytests-expected/001.json)). These obviously will always vary, so `testApp()` tells you there are diffs in all of the JSON snapshots (but none in the PNG ones). Since the PNG snapshots don’t change and the JSON diffs make it clear that only these parts changed, maybe that’s ok. But I was wondering: it may be nice to let users set a diff ignore of some kind (or we do it for specific keywords like session and nonce, and let users opt into it). 

